<title>MEXICO: Mexico's &quot;El Pollo Loco&quot; to expand abroad.</title>
<headline>Mexico's &quot;El Pollo Loco&quot; to expand abroad.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The popular Mexican fast-food chain &quot;El Pollo Loco,&quot; or the Crazy Chicken, said on Wednesday it plans to franchise hundreds more restaurants outside Mexico in the coming years.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to enter Argentina, Chile and Europe,&quot; the director of the privately-held restaurant chain, Jorge Gerardo Medina Garza, told Reuters.</p>
<p>There are currently 58 Pollo Locos in Mexico and 282 in the United States, Medina Garza said.</p>
<p>The company plans to franchise about 320 new restaurants in the United States in the next four to five years. In the next two years it plans to franchise four restaurants each in Chile and Argentina, 15 in Spain, and 10 each in France, Germany and Italy.</p>
<p>He said the firm is not opening new franchises in Mexico right now because of the weak economy.</p>
<p>-- Jacqueline Lerma, Monterrey bureau, (528) 345-7677</p>
